course: dictionary
lesson: 3408
title: Explorer: someone who finds out about the unknown
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An explorer is a person who travels to unknown or little-known places to find out what is there. The words around it give you clues: «Explorers travelled into the unknown and brought back descriptions, so mapmakers could fill in the gaps.» The explorers went where nobody had mapped, so the word must mean someone who goes to find things out.
explain: The word comes from explore, which means to look around carefully to learn about something. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: «Explorers were brave and skilled» still makes sense if you think of them as people who travel to find out about new places.
explain: Explorer also has other uses. Anyone who likes to look around and discover new things can be an explorer, like a child who loves finding creatures in a rock pool. In a computer, a file explorer is a program for finding files, so the context always tells you which meaning is meant.
explain: Look out for phrases that give more clues: «a polar explorer» travels to the cold regions near the North or South Pole, «a space explorer» travels beyond Earth, and «a famous explorer» is someone many people have heard of.
fact: An explorer travels to unknown or little-known places to find out about them.
fact: «A polar explorer» explores the cold regions near the North or South Pole.
fact: «Explorers were brave and skilled, but their voyages also opened the way for colonies that took land from local peoples.»
fact: Places explorers reached were rarely empty: people already lived there, with names for every river and mountain.
fact: French explorers and settlers founded Québec in 1608 and traded furs with First Nations across the country.
exercise: «Explorers travelled into the unknown and brought back descriptions.» What is an explorer? | A computer program that finds files | *A person who travels to unknown or little-known places to find out about them | A person who sells maps in a shop
exercise: What does a file explorer mean in a computer? | A ship that sails to new lands | A map of the moon | A kind of brave dog | *A program for finding files
exercise: «Explorers travelled into the unknown and brought back descriptions.» Find and copy the word that tells you the places were not known to anyone. | brought | *unknown | descriptions | travelled
test: What does «a polar explorer» mean? | A dog that sleeps on rugs | Someone who loves football | *Someone who explores the cold regions near the North or South Pole | A person who sells ice creams
test: «Explorers were brave and skilled, but their voyages also opened the way for colonies that took land from local peoples.» What does this sentence show? | Brave explorers never made mistakes | Colonies were always empty land | Explorers only ever helped local people | *Explorers' journeys could also harm the people already living there
exam: Why does the word discovered tell only one side of the story? | *Because the people already living there had their own names for every river and mountain | Because nobody lived anywhere before explorers came | Because the explorers never wrote anything down | Because maps were always right
